-- M19 On-Call Triage §3.2 Phase E — the platform-floor protocol catalog seed (D4 / D7 / §1.1).
--
-- 28 `triage_protocol` rows with `organization_id IS NULL` + `is_system_locked = true`, and their 111
-- ordered `triage_protocol_question` rows. §1.1 requires "≥ 25 platform-floor protocols covering the
-- hospice industry's high-frequency after-hours presentations" and enumerates 26; the floor ships 28
-- because two of those 26 split (see the header of
-- `apps/backend/src/modules/19-oncall/lifecycle/protocol-catalog.ts`, which is the SOURCE this file was
-- generated from and which `apps/backend/__tests__/oncall-protocol-catalog.test.ts` asserts this file
-- still matches).
--
-- WHY THIS IS ITS OWN MIGRATION AND NOT PART OF 0107. The seed encodes `red_flag_match` — the D5 predicate
-- the server evaluates every answer against — and that predicate's SHAPE is owned by the protocol engine
-- (M19-T03), not by the schema (M19-T02). Seeding rows whose predicate shape the evaluator had not yet
-- fixed would have frozen a guess into 111 rows.
--
-- FLOOR-PLUS-OVERLAY (D4, the M21 `comfort_kit_template` precedent): migration 0108's SELECT policy admits
-- `organization_id IS NULL`, so every tenant READS these rows; its INSERT/UPDATE policies admit only the
-- tenant's own unlocked rows, so no tenant can edit or disable one. That is what makes D7's four mandatory-
-- escalation protocols (`unresponsive_patient`, `suicidal_ideation`, `suspected_abuse_neglect`,
-- `emergency_drug_request_unfulfillable`) undisableable by tenant configuration rather than merely
-- discouraged: an agency under staffing pressure cannot clear a flag on a row it has no policy to write.
--
-- IDS ARE DETERMINISTIC (`00000000-0019-0000-…` for protocols, `00000000-0019-0001-PPQQ-…` for questions)
-- and both INSERTs are `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`, so the seed is re-runnable and a later migration can amend
-- one row by id without a lookup.
--
-- SNOMED: the `snomed_code` values are the floor's PROVISIONAL mapping. The corpus carries no loaded SNOMED
-- value set yet (M38 declares the `snomed` code-system kind and nothing populates it), so only unambiguous,
-- widely-published concept ids are used and every operational protocol carries 74964007 ("Other"). A wrong
-- code is indistinguishable from a right one downstream — it flows into `triage_call.chief_complaint_snomed`
-- and the §4.3 feature DTO — so an explicit generic is the honest placeholder. M19-T07's catalog route
-- validates each code through M38 before a tenant may reference it.

